OL,3,GNEWSAThe winners of Lincolnshire Make a
OL,4,ADifference
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who dedicated more than 40 years
OL,7,Fto a wildlife charity group, a woman
OL,8,Fwho restored dignity to those buried in
OL,9,Ftwo cemeteries and a cockapoo called
OL,10,FRosie have been recognised this year by
OL,11,FBBC Radio Lincolnshire at the annual
OL,12,FMake A Difference Awards.
OL,14,FEight individuals were handed awards
OL,15,Fwhich were designed to recognise those
OL,16,Fwho have made outstanding contributions
OL,17,Fto their communities.
OL,19,FThe event was held at the International
OL,20,FBomber Command Centre in Lincoln.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
